<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch post NLG 10.2 bln Q2 current account surplus.</title>
<headline>Dutch post NLG 10.2 bln Q2 current account surplus.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Netherlands posted a 10.2 billion guilder current account surplus in the second quarter of 1996, the Dutch central bank said.</p>
<p>The bank published the following figures for the current account of the Dutch balance of payments:</p>
<p>DUTCH CURRENT ACCOUNT BALANCE  Q3 96  Q2 96  Q1 96  Q4 95  Q3 95</p>
<p> Goods				  n.a.   9.65   8.68   9.36   8.34</p>
<p> Services			    -1.10   3.17   0.61   1.58  -0.36</p>
<p> Income				 3.36   0.25  -0.77   1.30   2.08</p>
<p> Current transfers		 -2.42  -2.85  -2.29  -3.49  -2.42</p>
<p> Current account balance	  n.a.  10.22   6.24   8.75   7.65</p>
<p>NOTES - All figures in billions of guilders. Negative sign denotes deficit.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
